{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Give SwiftUI views a tracker through the environment, and track what they do with view modifiers.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenViewed"],"anchor":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"title":"Enumerations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenKey"],"anchor":"Enumerations"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this module to track events from SwiftUI views on Apple platforms; elsewhere it builds empty."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Set a tracker once, at the root of the views, with "},{"code":"tracker(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and read it in any view below"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"code":"@Environment(\\.tracker)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A button’s action can track through it, which a "},{"code":"withTracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binding can’t reach, since SwiftUI runs actions on tasks of its own. Until a tracker is set, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"environment’s tracker tracks through the one "},{"code":"Tracker.bootstrap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" made the process’s default, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with none it drops each event, warning once per call site. In a preview it is "},{"code":"Tracker.noOp","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a preview tracks nothing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The modifiers track through the environment’s tracker, once per trigger, and record the place"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they are applied as the call site. "},{"code":"trackOnAppear(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks each time a view appears,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"trackOnTap(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" each tap beside the view’s own action, and "},{"code":"trackChange(of:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" each new value."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"trackScreen(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks "},{"code":"ScreenViewed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" each time the view appears, and puts a tracker enriched"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the screen’s "},{"code":"ScreenKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in the environment inside it, so every event tracked from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"screen carries its name:"}]},{"code":["import SwiftUI","import Traffluent","","@Event","struct CartOpened {}","","@Event","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Int","}","","struct CartView: View {","    @Environment(\\.tracker) private var tracker","","    var body: some View {","        List {","            Button(\"Check out\") {","                tracker.track(CheckoutStarted(cartSize: 3))  \/\/ its record's context[ScreenKey.self] is \"Cart\"","            }","        }","        .trackOnAppear(CartOpened())","    }","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","let root = CartView()","    .trackScreen(\"Cart\")  \/\/ tracks ScreenViewed(screen: \"Cart\") each time it appears","    .tracker(tracker)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Apply ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackScreen(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" where the screen’s view is placed, as above, not in the view’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a view’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Environment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads the environment around it, which its own body’s modifiers don’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Where UIKit has traits, the environment’s tracker is the same value as UIKit’s trait"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking"},{"type":"text","text":"), so SwiftUI views hosted in UIKit read the scene’s tracker. For UIKit and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"AppKit views, see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"To track screens without a modifier on each, see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/automaticscreentracking"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The guide"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers all three frameworks."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"API","anchor":"API"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The documentation site is built on Linux, where this module’s views aren’t there, so their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbols have no pages of their own here. Their doc comments are in the sources, and Xcode shows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them for an Apple target. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenViewed","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenKey","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" build on every platform, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracking plan or a collector off Apple platforms can name them.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Setting the tracker","anchor":"Setting-the-tracker"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"EnvironmentValues.tracker","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View.tracker(_:)"}]}]}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Tracking from views","anchor":"Tracking-from-views"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"View.trackOnAppear(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"View.trackOnTap(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View.trackChange(of:_:)"}]}]}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Screens","anchor":"Screens"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View.trackScreen(_:)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenViewed","type":"reference"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenKey","type":"reference"}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftUITracking"}],"role":"collection","title":"SwiftUITracking","externalID":"SwiftUITracking","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftuitracking"]}],"references":{"doc://SwiftUITracking/documentation/SwiftUITracking/ScreenViewed":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftuitracking\/screenviewed","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenViewed","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenViewed","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenViewed","title":"ScreenViewed","abstract":[{"text":"Someone viewed the screen named ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenViewed\/screen"},{"text":": what ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackScreen(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tracks each time its view","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"appears.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftUITracking/documentation/SwiftUITracking/ScreenKey":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenKey"}],"title":"ScreenKey","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenKey"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking\/ScreenKey","url":"\/documentation\/swiftuitracking\/screenkey","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ServiceContext"},{"type":"text","text":" key of the screen an event was tracked from: the name given to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackScreen(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/trackingfromviews":{"title":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UI